  "title": "Workload Capture/Replay Request Schemas Renamed",
  "summary": "The request body schemas for Cloud SQL Admin API's workload capture and replay methods have been renamed, requiring updates to client code.",
  "details": "Developers using the Cloud SQL Admin API's workload capture and replay features should note a breaking change: the request body schemas for `workloadCaptures.start`, `workloadCaptures.startReplay`, `workloadCaptures.stop`, and `workloadCaptures.stopReplay` methods have been renamed. The previous schemas, such as `SqlWorkloadCapturesStartRequest` and `SqlWorkloadCapturesStartReplayRequest`, have been removed. You must now use the new schema names: `WorkloadCapturesStartRequest`, `WorkloadCapturesStartReplayRequest`, `WorkloadCapturesStopRequest`, and `WorkloadCapturesStopReplayRequest` respectively. This is a direct rename, so the underlying structure of the request bodies remains consistent, but your client code will need to be updated to reference the new schema names.",
